  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the given figure, an inductor&nbsp;and resistor are connected in series with a battery of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>emf</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math>&nbsp;volt.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;represents the maximum rate at which the energy is stored in the magnetic field&nbsp;(inductor). The numerical value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;will be _____.</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"assets\\qt0038_0d642c32a5f6.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 186px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "25",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the current flowing through an L-R circuit is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>E</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>The energy stored within the inductor can be calculated as follows:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>induction&#160;</mtext></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>L</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>L</mi><mfrac><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The rate of change of energy stored within the inductor is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>induction&#160;</mtext></msub></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>For maximum rate,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From equation (3) and (4), it can be written that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>R</mi></mstyle></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>L</mi></mstyle></mfrac></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>L</mi></mstyle></mfrac></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>5</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>From equation (3) and (5), it can be written,&nbsp;under maximum energy stored condition for the circuit, that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>induction&#160;</mtext></msub></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Substitute the values of the resistance and compare with the given expression to obtain the values of the parameters.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>50</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Hence, the required ratio is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}